    "total_efficiency_score": 696.85,
    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-upside speed threats and favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms. **Seiya Suzuki** leads our lineup with a 67.36 efficiency score, bolstered by a prime #2 hole opportunity and a favorable matchup against Seth Lugo. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (64.10) and **Corbin Carroll** (64.88) are our primary engines for stolen bases; **Brice Turang** benefits from the combination of a leadoff spot and a high probability of success on the basepaths against a slower-delivering Taj Bradley, while **Corbin Carroll** remains an auto-start despite the tough matchup against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, as his elite speed profile provides a floor even when offensive production is difficult to project. **Isaac Paredes** (64.27) also earns a strong start, capitalizing on a platoon advantage against Michael King.\n\nWe continue to prioritize power-speed combinations, but the benching of **Zach McKinstry** (42.77) serves as the primary optimizer decision of the day. While **Zach McKinstry** carries a decent floor, he was sidelined in favor of the higher-ceiling profiles of **Max Muncy** (62.89) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (60.58), both of whom benefit significantly from wind-aided conditions and advantageous platoon splits against Bennett. We remain cautious regarding **Gabriel Moreno** and **Austin Riley**, both of whom are battling elite opposing arms; while their raw talent dictates their inclusion, their scores are anchored by the formidable threat posed by Yoshinobu Yamamoto and Gerrit Cole. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that several of our starters, including **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Isaac Paredes**, are currently designated as \"Lineup Pending.\" Should any of these players fail to appear in their projected batting order slots, we will re-evaluate their efficiency relative to available depth. As always, our long-term strategy for the 5x5 Roto standings necessitates patience with **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** as they recover on the IL, keeping our focus strictly on maximizing daily production from our active core to close the gap in the stolen base category.",
